ntdll, wow64, wow64win, winemac: 32-bit programs in a window above 4 GB

A 32-bit Windows program expects the first 4 GB of the address space. macOS gives a native
arm64 process nothing below 4 GB, so 32-bit programs could not run at all in this runtime.

Here a 32-bit process gets its 4 GB as a window higher up, at 1 TB. The window's base is a
multiple of 4 GB, and that is what keeps this small: an address in the window, cut to 32 bits,
is the address the program sees, so everything that already truncates a pointer for 32-bit code
is right as it is. Only the other direction, a 32-bit value becoming a real pointer, needs the
base, and Wine's 32-to-64 layer does that through two macros.

Where the window is: 4 GB to 6 GB holds the process itself, 6 GB to 63 GB is the system's shared
library region (nothing can be mapped in its gaps) and 63 GB to 448 GB is a guard; 1 TB is free.

dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
- reserves the window in every process (address space only);
- knows a process is 32-bit when the first image mapped, before the main image is known, is a
  32-bit one, and from then on places every allocation and image with a 32-bit limit inside the
  window; a 32-bit image's own base (0x400000 for most programs) is that address in the window;
- maps the shared data page a second time at window + 0x7ffe0000, where 32-bit code reads it;
- nothing about memory changes in a process that is not 32-bit.

include/basetsd.h
- in the Unix libraries, ULongToPtr/UlongToPtr add the window's base (zero unless the process
  is 32-bit); WINE_WOW_WINDOW_PTR64 does the same for a 64-bit field a 32-bit program filled.

dlls/wow64, dlls/wow64win
- the same two macros with the base; address limits are compared on the 32-bit value;
- window messages whose lparam is a pointer (win32u's table) get the base, as do the generic
  one-, two- and window-parameter calls whose arguments are pointers;
- a process attribute too large for its value field is a pointer.

dlls/ntdll/locale.c
- the 32-bit side writes the code page pointers into the 64-bit process block with the base.

dlls/winemac.drv
- param_ptr() takes pointers the 32-bit side passes in 64-bit fields.

dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_arm64.c
- a fault inside a system call is traced with its library, function and callers: such a fault
  is usually a pointer that still lacks the base, and this is how the place is found.

The emulator's side is patches/fex/0011. Checked with tests/runtime/suite32.c (threads,
exceptions, generated code, window messages, drawing, child processes) and Microsoft's 32-bit
Visual C++ set-up program.

diff --git a/include/basetsd.h b/include/basetsd.h
--- a/include/basetsd.h
+++ b/include/basetsd.h
@@ -288,6 +288,32 @@
 #define UlongToHandle(ul)       ULongToHandle(ul)
 #define UintToPtr(ui)           UIntToPtr(ui)
 #define UlongToPtr(ul)          ULongToPtr(ul)
+
+/* FineWine 32-bit: on macOS/arm64 a 32-bit program's memory is a 4 GB window at a base that
+ * is a multiple of 4 GB (dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c). In the Unix libraries of such a process,
+ * a 32-bit value that is a pointer gets the base; NULL, atoms and ordinals (below 64K) and
+ * the top 64K (-1 and friends) are not addresses. The base is 0 in every other process. */
+#if defined(WINE_UNIX_LIB) && defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__) && defined(_WIN64)
+extern unsigned __int64 __wine_wow_window_base;
+static inline void *__wine_wow_window_ptr( ULONG32 ul )
+{
+    if (ul < 0x10000 || ul >= 0xffff0000) return (void *)(ULONG_PTR)ul;
+    return (void *)((ULONG_PTR)ul | __wine_wow_window_base);
+}
+/* The same for a pointer a 32-bit program stored in a 64-bit field, where it has no base. */
+static inline void *__wine_wow_window_ptr64( unsigned __int64 value )
+{
+    if (value >= 0x10000 && value < 0xffff0000) value |= __wine_wow_window_base;
+    return (void *)(ULONG_PTR)value;
+}
+#undef ULongToPtr
+#undef UlongToPtr
+#define ULongToPtr(ul) __wine_wow_window_ptr( ul )
+#define UlongToPtr(ul) __wine_wow_window_ptr( ul )
+#define WINE_WOW_WINDOW_PTR64(value) __wine_wow_window_ptr64( value )
+#else
+#define WINE_WOW_WINDOW_PTR64(value) ((void *)(ULONG_PTR)(value))
+#endif
 
 typedef LONG_PTR SHANDLE_PTR;
 typedef ULONG_PTR HANDLE_PTR;
